(703, 'CH40-R004', 40, 65, 'CAMERA_PLACEMENT', 'Table No. (1): VSS Requirements', 4, 'Inside vault / safe compartment', 'Observation View', 'Video Surveillance System (IP Cameras)', 'Location: Inside vault / safe compartment | Field of View: OBSERVATION | Remarks: IP66 mobile camera', 'Install IP camera covering Inside vault / safe compartment achieving OBSERVATION View (IP66 mobile camera).', 'IP66 mobile camera', 'SIRA prior written approval required for pixel-density (PPM) alternative or exception.', 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 40: Transport of Money and Valuable Materials (Cash-in-Transit (CIT) Armored Vehicles)', 137, 137, 'VERIFIED'),
(704, 'CH40-R005', 40, 65, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 5, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Vehicle GPS Tracking & Mobile DVR', '3-Section Armored Vehicle Body (B4 Minimum Armoring): Vehicle must be divided into 3 compartments (engine, crew cabin, vault) with minimum B4 ballistic armor and bullet-resistant glass providing >=200° field of vision.', '3-Section Armored Vehicle Body (B4 Minimum Armoring) — Vehicle must be divided into 3 compartments (engine, crew cabin, vault) with minimum B4 ballistic armor and bullet-resistant glass providing >=200° field of vision.', 'Vehicle must be divided into 3 compartments (engine, crew cabin, vault) with minimum B4 ballistic armor and bullet-resistant glass providing >=200° field of vision.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 40: Transport of Money and Valuable Materials (Cash-in-Transit (CIT) Armored Vehicles)', 135, 135, 'VERIFIED'),
(705, 'CH40-R006', 40, 65, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 6, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Vehicle GPS Tracking & Mobile DVR', 'Run-Flat Tires (>=100 km at 80 km/h) & 60x60 cm Escape Hatch: Equip all wheels with run-flat tires capable of traveling >=100 km and a roof/floor emergency hatch of at least 60x60 cm.', 'Run-Flat Tires (>=100 km at 80 km/h) & 60x60 cm Escape Hatch — Equip all wheels with run-flat tires capable of traveling >=100 km and a roof/floor emergency hatch of at least 60x60 cm.', 'Equip all wheels with run-flat tires capable of traveling >=100 km and a roof/floor emergency hatch of at least 60x60 cm.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 40: Transport of Money and Valuable Materials (Cash-in-Transit (CIT) Armored Vehicles)', 136, 136, 'VERIFIED'),
(706, 'CH40-R007', 40, 65, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 7, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'SIRA-Approved Lock (Standard 2320:2012)', 'Biometric + Digital Double-Open Vault Lock & Crew ID Engine Start: Vault door requires dual authentication (biometric + digital code); engine ignition requires authorized crew ID card and speed limiter.', 'Biometric + Digital Double-Open Vault Lock & Crew ID Engine Start — Vault door requires dual authentication (biometric + digital code); engine ignition requires authorized crew ID card and speed limiter.', 'Vault door requires dual authentication (biometric + digital code); engine ignition requires authorized crew ID card and speed limiter.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 40: Transport of Money and Valuable Materials (Cash-in-Transit (CIT) Armored Vehicles)', 136, 136, 'VERIFIED'),
(707, 'CH40-R008', 40, 65, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 8, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Vehicle GPS Tracking & Mobile DVR', 'Live GPS Tracking, Panic Buttons & SIRA Connectivity: Connect vehicle GPS, panic buttons, and mobile DVR to the CIT Operations Center and SIRA.', 'Live GPS Tracking, Panic Buttons & SIRA Connectivity — Connect vehicle GPS, panic buttons, and mobile DVR to the CIT Operations Center and SIRA.', 'Connect vehicle GPS, panic buttons, and mobile DVR to the CIT Operations Center and SIRA.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 40: Transport of Money and Valuable Materials (Cash-in-Transit (CIT) Armored Vehicles)', 137, 137, 'VERIFIED'),
(708, 'CH41-R001', 41, 66, 'CAMERA_PLACEMENT', 'Table No. (1): VSS Requirements', 1, 'Front road view (on hazardous material transport trucks)', 'Observation View', 'Video Surveillance System (IP Cameras)', 'Location: Front road view (on hazardous material transport trucks) | Field of View: OBSERVATION | Remarks: Mobile DVR recording at >=30 fps', 'Install IP camera covering Front road view (on hazardous material transport trucks) achieving OBSERVATION View (Mobile DVR recording at >=30 fps).', 'Mobile DVR recording at >=30 fps', 'SIRA prior written approval required for pixel-density (PPM) alternative or exception.', 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 41: Vehicle Safety and Protection (Regulated Commercial and Hazardous Transport Vehicles)', 138, 138, 'VERIFIED'),
(709, 'CH41-R002', 41, 66, 'CAMERA_PLACEMENT', 'Table No. (1): VSS Requirements', 2, 'Rear / tank valve and unloading zone (on hazardous material trucks)', 'Observation View', 'Video Surveillance System (IP Cameras)', 'Location: Rear / tank valve and unloading zone (on hazardous material trucks) | Field of View: OBSERVATION | Remarks: Explosion-proof IP66 cameras at >=30 fps', 'Install IP camera covering Rear / tank valve and unloading zone (on hazardous material trucks) achieving OBSERVATION View (Explosion-proof IP66 cameras at >=30 fps).', 'Explosion-proof IP66 cameras at >=30 fps', 'SIRA prior written approval required for pixel-density (PPM) alternative or exception.', 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 41: Vehicle Safety and Protection (Regulated Commercial and Hazardous Transport Vehicles)', 138, 138, 'VERIFIED'),
(710, 'CH41-R003', 41, 66, 'CAMERA_PLACEMENT', 'Table No. (1): VSS Requirements', 3, 'Left and right sides of hazardous transport vehicle', 'Detection View', 'Video Surveillance System (IP Cameras)', 'Location: Left and right sides of hazardous transport vehicle | Field of View: DETECTION', 'Install IP camera covering Left and right sides of hazardous transport vehicle achieving DETECTION View.', NULL, 'SIRA prior written approval required for pixel-density (PPM) alternative or exception.', 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 41: Vehicle Safety and Protection (Regulated Commercial and Hazardous Transport Vehicles)', 138, 138, 'VERIFIED'),
(711, 'CH41-R004', 41, 66, 'CAMERA_PLACEMENT', 'Table No. (1): VSS Requirements', 4, 'Inside driver cabin (on hazardous material trucks)', 'Identification View', 'Video Surveillance System (IP Cameras)', 'Location: Inside driver cabin (on hazardous material trucks) | Field of View: IDENTIFICATION', 'Install IP camera covering Inside driver cabin (on hazardous material trucks) achieving IDENTIFICATION View.', NULL, 'SIRA prior written approval required for pixel-density (PPM) alternative or exception.', 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 41: Vehicle Safety and Protection (Regulated Commercial and Hazardous Transport Vehicles)', 138, 138, 'VERIFIED'),
(712, 'CH41-R005', 41, 66, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 5, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Vehicle GPS Tracking & Mobile DVR', 'SIRA-Approved Vehicle Tracking System: Install SIRA-approved GPS tracking device on rental cars, hazardous material trucks, safari vehicles, and fuel tankers.', 'SIRA-Approved Vehicle Tracking System — Install SIRA-approved GPS tracking device on rental cars, hazardous material trucks, safari vehicles, and fuel tankers.', 'Install SIRA-approved GPS tracking device on rental cars, hazardous material trucks, safari vehicles, and fuel tankers.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 41: Vehicle Safety and Protection (Regulated Commercial and Hazardous Transport Vehicles)', 138, 138, 'VERIFIED'),
(713, 'CH42-R001', 42, 67, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 1, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Vehicle GPS Tracking & Mobile DVR', 'Use Licensed CIT Company & SIRA-Approved Cash Bags: Cash and valuables transfers exceeding regulatory thresholds must use SIRA-licensed CIT companies, armored vehicles, and SIRA-approved security bags equipped with GPS tracking and ink-staining/neutralization technology.', 'Use Licensed CIT Company & SIRA-Approved Cash Bags — Cash and valuables transfers exceeding regulatory thresholds must use SIRA-licensed CIT companies, armored vehicles, and SIRA-approved security bags equipped with GPS tracking and ink-staining/neutralization technology.', 'Cash and valuables transfers exceeding regulatory thresholds must use SIRA-licensed CIT companies, armored vehicles, and SIRA-approved security bags equipped with GPS tracking and ink-staining/neutralization technology.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 42: Transfer and Delivery of Money (Transfer and Delivery of Money Operations)', 139, 139, 'VERIFIED'),
(714, 'CH42-R002', 42, 67, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 2, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'SIRA-Licensed Security Personnel', 'Mandatory Guard Escort & Identity Verification at Handover: Verify identity of CIT crew before handover in a camera-monitored zone; public transport or two-wheeled motorcycles must never be used to transfer cash.', 'Mandatory Guard Escort & Identity Verification at Handover — Verify identity of CIT crew before handover in a camera-monitored zone; public transport or two-wheeled motorcycles must never be used to transfer cash.', 'Verify identity of CIT crew before handover in a camera-monitored zone; public transport or two-wheeled motorcycles must never be used to transfer cash.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 42: Transfer and Delivery of Money (Transfer and Delivery of Money Operations)', 139, 139, 'VERIFIED'),
(715, 'CH43-R001', 43, 68, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 1, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Wireless Guard Communication & Smart App', 'SIRA-Approved Wireless Communication Device: Provide every on-duty security guard with a SIRA-approved wireless communication device linked to the company\'s operations room.', 'SIRA-Approved Wireless Communication Device — Provide every on-duty security guard with a SIRA-approved wireless communication device linked to the company\'s operations room.', 'Provide every on-duty security guard with a SIRA-approved wireless communication device linked to the company\'s operations room.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 43: Communication and Communicating Requirements for Security Guard Service Providers (Security Guard Service Providers)', 140, 140, 'VERIFIED'),
(716, 'CH43-R002', 43, 68, 'OTHER_SECURITY_SYSTEM', 'Table No. (2): Other Security Requirements', 2, 'Establishment-Wide / Specified Area', NULL, 'Wireless Guard Communication & Smart App', 'SIRA-Approved Smart Guard Application: Install and operate the SIRA-approved smart application on the communication device for attendance, patrol verification, and emergency incident reporting.', 'SIRA-Approved Smart Guard Application — Install and operate the SIRA-approved smart application on the communication device for attendance, patrol verification, and emergency incident reporting.', 'Install and operate the SIRA-approved smart application on the communication device for attendance, patrol verification, and emergency incident reporting.', NULL, 'MANDATORY', NULL, 'Part Three', 'Chapter 43: Communication and Communicating Requirements for Security Guard Service Providers (Security Guard Service Providers)', 140, 140, 'VERIFIED');
INSERT INTO `source_citations` (`id`, `entity_type`, `entity_code`, `part_name`, `chapter_name`, `section_name`, `table_name`, `row_sn`, `pdf_page`, `printed_page`, `excerpt`) VALUES
(1, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-01', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Establishment', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '1', 6, 6, 'It includes vital sectors, important complexes and the like, specified in accordance with the provisions of the Executive Regulations of Law No. (12) of 2016 regarding the regulation of the security industry in the Emirate of Dubai.'),
(2, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-02', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Establishment Entrances', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '2', 6, 6, 'All entrances and exits to the establishment, including emergency exits.'),
(3, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-03', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Establishment Corridors', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '3', 6, 6, 'All corridors which are used by visitors or residents of residential buildings, including internal and external service corridors in the establishment.'),
(4, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-04', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Cash and Reception Counters', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '4', 6, 6, 'Includes all reception, service, assistance and cash desks in the establishment.'),
(5, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-05', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Stores', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '5', 6, 6, 'the facilities used for storage.'),
(6, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-06', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Warehouses', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '6', 6, 6, 'the facilities that include multiple warehouses designated for storage.'),
(7, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-07', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Vehicle Entrances', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '7', 6, 6, 'include all entrances and exits designated for vehicle movement into the establishment or its annexes.'),
(8, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-08', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Camera View Range (Field of view)', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '8', 6, 6, 'The visual range that is covered by the camera and displayed on the surveillance screen.'),
(9, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-09', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Standard Target', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '9', 6, 6, 'The object\'s visibility scale at a height of 1.6 meters, represented by a human body or a standard test target.'),
(10, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-10', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Image Element Density (Pixel Density)', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '10', 6, 6, 'The pixel count per meter at the standard target.'),
(11, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-11', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Vehicle License Plate View Range (Number Plate Recognition)', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '11', 6, 6, 'The visibility of a vehicle license plate measuring 330 x 160 mm.'),
(12, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-12', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Inspection View', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '12', 6, 6, 'The range used to analyze facial expressions of individuals (targets), where the face must be the most prominent element in the image.'),
(13, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-13', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Identification View', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '13', 6, 6, 'The identification visibility range is the range used to identify previously unknown individuals (targets) upon entering the establishment.'),
(14, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-14', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Recognition View', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '14', 6, 6, 'It is used to identify and track previously identified individuals (targets).'),
(15, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-15', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Observation View', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '15', 6, 6, 'It is used to control and direct crowds, gatherings, and public events.'),
(16, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-16', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Detection View', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '16', 6, 6, 'It is used to detect basic features such as the nature of movement, direction, and general appearance.'),
(17, 'DEFINITION', 'DEF-17', 'Definitions', 'Official Definitions Table', 'Monitoring View', 'Definitions Table (Page 6)', '17', 6, 6, 'It is used to detect the presence of targets without recognition for early warning purposes.'),
(18, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '1', 8, 8, 'They must be in color.'),
(19, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-02', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '2', 8, 8, 'The camera resolution must be at least 1080p Full HD.'),
(20, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-03', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '3', 8, 8, 'The variable bit rate feature must be enabled, without using a fixed bit rate and without specifying a maximum speed.'),
(21, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-04', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '4', 8, 8, 'They must be compatible with all the standard security system management software available on the market or capable of direct connection to known standard systems.'),
(22, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-05', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '5', 8, 8, 'The signal-to-noise ratio must be at least 48 dB.'),
(23, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-06', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '6', 8, 8, 'The cameras must be clearly visible and not hidden.'),
(24, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-07', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '7', 8, 8, 'The cameras must be designed and manufactured to operate continuously without interruption.'),
(25, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-08', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '8', 8, 8, 'Cameras or enclosures for outdoor use must have a rating of at least IP66 to ensure continuous operation in an outdoor environment'),
(26, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-09', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '9', 8, 8, 'A Dynamic Wide Range (WDR) is required for any camera facing a natural or artificial light source, direct or reflected from polished surfaces, and the WDR must be at least 110 dB or equivalent'),
(27, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-10', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '10', 8, 8, 'Auto Iris feature must be used for locations where lighting varies according to the time of day.'),
(28, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-11', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '11', 8, 8, 'Infrared (IR) light is required, with the ability to automatically switch to monochrome night photography when visible light fades.'),
(29, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CAM-12', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'First: Cameras', 'Digital/IP Cameras', '12', 8, 8, 'Cameras installed at height of 4 meters and above shall have remote zoom and focus ability.'),
(30, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '1', 9, 9, 'Only digital recording devices must be used'),
(31, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-02', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '2', 9, 9, 'The recording resolution must be at least 1080p Full HD.'),
(32, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-03', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '3', 9, 9, 'The live view resolution must be at least 1080p Full HD for single-camera viewing, and at least 2 CIF per camera for multiple-screen viewing.'),
(33, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-04', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '4', 9, 9, 'It must be capable of performing the three basic functions simultaneously: (1) live view, (2) recording, and (3) playback of previous recordings, without any degraded or negatively impacted performance of any of these functions.'),
(34, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-05', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '5', 9, 9, 'Live view must be at least 25 frames per second for each camera.'),
(35, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-09', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '9', 9, 9, 'Both continuous and non-continuous recording must be available. (Non-continuous recording is associated with a specific event, such as motion or a signal from an external device, such as intruder detection system sensors.) In the case of non-continuous recording, the device must be capable of recording scenes before and after the event, lasting at least ten (10) seconds. These features must be available so that they can be activated for all cameras connected to the recording device individually (i.e., they can be activated for each camera separately).'),
(36, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-10', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications & C. Recording Duration', 'Recording Retention & Frame Rate', '10', 10, 10, 'Minimum non-continuous motion-activated recording setting: No less than 70% of the day for each camera, no less than 10 frames per second for each camera, and no less than 31 days. C. Recording Duration and Quality: The recording must be kept for at least 31 days, at high quality, and at a frame rate of at least 10 frames per second.'),
(37, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-11', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '11', 10, 10, 'The recording devices must be computed with 20% extra capacity.'),
(38, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-REC-17', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — A. General Specifications', 'Recording Devices (NVR/DVR)', '17', 10, 10, '16. Software Development Kit (SDK) shall be made available and to be provided to SIRA upon request. 17. It shall be compatible with ONVIF 2.0 standards. 18. It shall support live streaming through the Real Time Streaming Protocol (RTSP). 19. It shall support the Central Time feature (Network Time Protocol (NTP)). 20–26. It shall support alarms/notifications for disk failure, disk full, recording On/Off, schedule change, camera malfunction, user login with ID, and running pulse signal.'),
(39, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-VREC-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Second: Recording devices — B. Additional Specifications of Vehicles Recording Devices', 'Vehicle Recording Devices', '1', 11, 11, '1. The ability to record, display, and extract recordings simultaneously. 2. A display screen must be installed within the driver\'s and assistant\'s line of sight. 3. The recording device must be stored in a clean, secure location, protected from theft, vandalism, or tampering. 4. The device must be specifically designed for vehicles. 5. It must be equipped with a solid-state drive (SSD). 6. The system must be connected to the vehicle\'s backup battery. 7. All system cables must be in secure cases.'),
(40, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-MON-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Third: Display devices', 'Surveillance Displays & Monitors', '1', 11, 11, '1. All monitors shall be of high operational specifications to be suitable for continuous operations without interruptions for a period not less than three years (Monitors must be designed for continuous work 24/7 - 365 days). 2. The monitor\'s resolution should not be less than Full HD 1080p. 3. Monitors must be specific to surveillance and not television screens. 4. At least two monitors must be available to each security systems operator, the size of each shall not be less than 21 inches. 5. Wall monitors must be provided in the control rooms (The image size of each camera should not be less than 12 x 6.7 cm in the display monitor).'),
(41, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-MON-10', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Third: Display devices', 'Surveillance Displays & Monitors', '10', 12, 12, '9. Critical cameras must be always displayed at the center of the wall display. These cameras include cameras at entrances, reception and assistance desks, passenger drop-off areas, elevator lobbies and stairwells on the main floors, the main lobby, and any other cameras deemed important by the security officer or as directed by SIRA. 10. Standard cameras imaging must be displayed in the terminal areas of the full wall monitor in the form of sets of serial cameras, provided that the total cycle time does not exceed 60 seconds, and the number of sets does not exceed 6 sets. 11. Wall Monitors: The thickness of the outer frame of wall monitors shall not exceed 4 mm.'),
(42, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-CON-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Fourth: Connectors', 'Cables & Connectors', '1', 12, 12, '1. Where twisted pairs are used, the type used must contain a minimum of high-quality copper known as CAT 6. Remarks: Cables (copper clad aluminum) and (copper clad iron) are not allowed. 7. Exposed connections must be protected by plastic conduits for indoor use and metal conduits specially designed for outdoor use. 8. Connections to all wire terminals must be numbered, identified, and labeled. 10. The use of wireless networks for security systems is prohibited unless approved by the institution.'),
(43, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-NET-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Fifth: Network', 'Network Requirements', '2', 13, 13, '2. A separate, dedicated private network must be created and installed solely for security systems. 3. The network must have redundancy and sustainability characteristics, avoiding single, irreplaceable major breakpoints. 4. The backbone of the network must be equipped with a secondary backup line. 5. The network must be equipped with a network management system (NMS)... if the number of devices connected to the network exceeds 200 devices. 6. Consider dividing the network into segments and clusters if the number of devices connected to the network exceeds 200. 7. Compatible with IPv4 and IPv6. 8. An additional 20% of the total capacity must be calculated from the network system.'),
(44, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-UPS-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Sixth: Energy sources', 'Energy Sources & Backup Power (UPS)', '1', 14, 14, '1. Security systems must be powered by uninterruptible power supplies (UPS), capable of operating autonomously in the event of a power outage for at least 30 minutes. 2. All recording devices in VSS systems must be connected to a UPS. 3. The recording devices and UPS must be integrated so that the UPS can automatically shut down the recording devices when the remaining battery level in the UPS reaches 25% of the total charge (optional).'),
(45, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C1-VMS-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter One: Digital Systems Specifications (IP)', 'Seventh: Control and management', 'Control & Management Software (VMS / PSIM)', '1', 14, 14, '1. VMS surveillance system management software must be provided for any VSS system connected to 64 or more cameras or 4 or more recording devices. 2. Security features must be available to ensure control and security through passwords and multiple permissions. 3. Control and monitoring stations (workstations) must be ready, efficient, and dedicated to these tasks only. 4. When it is necessary to integrate different systems with security systems (such as integrating VSS systems with access control, alarms, and building management systems), PSIM security information management systems must be used after prior written approval from SIRA.'),
(46, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C2-ACS-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter Two: Specifications of Access Control Systems', 'First: General specifications & Second: Locking mechanisms', 'Access Control Systems', '1', 15, 15, 'First: 1. To be compatible with all fire alarm systems approved by the relevant authorities in the emirate. 2. to be centralized. 3. To be able to handle both analog and digital systems. Second: 1. To be self-opening in case of emergency and it is allowed the use of electromagnetic or electromechanical locks. 2. They must be self-locking in case of emergency and only electromechanical if installed on the following doors: Financial safes and safes contain valuable contents; Safes containing hazardous materials; Safes containing narcotics and restricted medications; Weapons and ammunition depots; Detention and quarantine facilities. Remarks: Any place where emergency self-locking locks are used and are likely to be operated by people, the lock must have a manual emergency release feature, and this feature must be used only on the secured side of the lock.'),
(47, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C2-ACS-02', 'Part One', 'Chapter Two: Specifications of Access Control Systems', 'Fourth: Control Panel & Fifth: Management and Control Software', 'Access Control Systems', '1', 16, 16, 'Fourth: 1. All control panels must be equipped with a backup battery to ensure continued operation during a main power outage for at least 4 hours. 2. Systems must be built based on communication over the digital network. 3. Must be able to save all operations internally when the connection to the central control system is lost, and to automatically complete the data update when the connection is restored. Fifth: 2. To retain login and logout details for all linked devices for a period of no less than one year. 4. It should contain an interactive electronic map to control the systems. 5. Complete software development kits (SDKs) must be provided.'),
(48, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C3-ALM-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter Three: Specifications for Alarm and Intruder Detection Systems', 'First: Sensors', 'Alarm & Intruder Detection', '1', 17, 17, 'All system components must be third generation at a minimum. First: Sensors: 1. The sensors field must cover protected areas so that no area can be breached to stop or disable the security system. 2. Dual-technology motion detectors, such as infrared and microwaves, should be used. 3. Vibration detection sensors must be used. 4. Drilling detection sensors must be used. 5. Glass break sensors must be used. 6. Panic buttons and keys must be provided for facility personnel to use in the event of an emergency, must be at a level that is easy to use and hidden. 7. Door Contact (For Normal and Fortified Doors).'),
(49, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C3-ALM-02', 'Part One', 'Chapter Three: Specifications for Alarm and Intruder Detection Systems', 'Second: Visual and audible alarm and warning devices & Third: Connectors', 'Alarm & Intruder Detection', '1', 17, 17, 'Second: 1. The alarm (audio and visual) must be installed, equipped with a loudspeaker, and a flashing light that attracts attention. 2. The device\'s ringing duration must be set for at least 5 minutes or until the alarm is reset. 3. The alarm (audio and visual) must be installed at a minimum of 110 dBA from a distance of 1 meter to be audible and its flashing visible from the outside. 4. The alarm (audio and visual) must be equipped with a backup battery that can operate for 8 continuous hours. Third: 1. Connectors must be wired. Wireless connection of sensors may only be used after obtaining prior written approval from SIRA. 2. Each sensor must be connected separately to the control and alarm panel and to a single zone. 5. The entire system must be equipped with a backup power supply (UPS) that will operate it in the event of a power outage for at least 8 hours.'),
(50, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C3-ALM-03', 'Part One', 'Chapter Three: Specifications for Alarm and Intruder Detection Systems', 'Fourth: Control and alarm panel & Fifth: System administrator', 'Alarm & Intruder Detection', '1', 18, 18, 'Fourth: 1. The Alarm system control panel must be approved by SIRA. 2. The control panel must be connected to the central alarm station. 3. Each sensor must be programmed individually with a separate zone. 5. To be connected to the facility\'s lighting control system so that it can turn on the lighting on site when an alarm is triggered. 6. Installed in a secure, hidden, and difficult-to-access location. 7. Keypad installed away from control panel and near entry/exit door. 8. Tamper detection on all parts. 9. The time allocated to disarm the Alarm system must not exceed one minute. If a longer time is required, prior written approval from the organization must be obtained. 10. The number of incorrect attempts to disable the Alarm system must not exceed three (3) consecutive attempts. 11. Equipped with a backup battery that can operate for 8 continuous hours.'),
(51, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C4-LCK-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter Four: Locks Specifications', 'First: General Specifications (Standard No. 2320:2012(E))', 'Locks & Resistance Standards', '1', 20, 20, 'Pry-resistant, puncture-resistant, and shear-resistant locks with high-quality security keys must be installed, based on Standard No. 2320:2012(E) Lock Standards, Fittings, Requirements, and Test Methods. 1. Force resistance on cylinder plug/locking mechanism >= 10 kN. 2. Torque resistance >= 20 Nm. 3. Lock pull resistance >= 70 kN. 4. Lock torsion resistance >= 1200 Nm. 5. Lock cutting resistance >= 70 kN. 6. Lock body impact resistance at low temperatures (-40°C, 6550 grams, 1400 mm). 7. Drilling resistance >= 4 minutes. 8. Cut resistance >= 4 minutes.'),
(52, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C5-GLS-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter Five: Specifications of Penetration-Resistant Glass', 'First: General Specifications', 'Penetration-Resistant Glass', '1', 20, 20, 'Piercing-resistant glass or the use of piercing-resistant films attached to a strong frame, on the facility\'s glass facades so that the glass resists penetration for at least 90 seconds.'),
(53, 'STANDARD', 'P1-C6-HVM-01', 'Part One', 'Chapter Six: HVM Barriers Specifications (External Perimeter Safety)', 'First to Fifth: HVM Types, Prior Approval & Light/Medium/Heavy Impact Ratings', 'Hostile Vehicle Mitigation (HVM)', '1', 21, 21, 'Second: HVM Types Based on Shape: 1. strong walls, 2. Bollards, 3. Road Blockers, 4. Planter boxes and containers, 5. Roadside assets and equipment, 6. Water pools and fountains, 7. Columns, 8. Landscape elements. Third: Operational types: 1. Movable HVM, 2. Fixed HVM. Fourth: Requirements: 1. SIRA approval (prior to implementation) must be obtained for the locations, design, and calculations of all types of HVM for each project. Fifth: Installation requirements: 1. Light: Vehicle weight 1,500 kg, 110 km/h, 90 degrees, Penetration distance: 0 meters. 2. Medium: Vehicle weight 7,500 kg, 80 km/h, 90 degrees, Penetration distance: 0 meters. 3. Heavy: Vehicle weight 32,000 kg (6x6), 80 km/h, 90 degrees, Penetration distance: 0 meters.'),
(54, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C2-COM-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Two: Remote Communication Requirements', 'Remote Linking to SIRA Monitoring Systems', 'Remote Communication & Monitoring', '1', 27, 27, '1. Connecting the VSS system to the system integrity monitoring service approved by SIRA (Installing a system for linking and following up the integrity of VSS). 2. Connecting the facility\'s alarm and intruder detection systems to SIRA approved alarm systems monitoring system. 3. Connecting the electronic registration systems for vehicle plate numbers to the system of linking and monitoring the electronic registration systems for vehicle plate numbers approved by SIRA.'),
(55, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C3-MGT-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Three: Management and Operation', 'Management and Operational Responsibilities', 'Management & Operation', '1', 27, 27, '1. An employee must be responsible for the facility\'s security systems. They must be familiar with the use and operation of the systems and perform all operational tasks, such as copying, searching, and uploading clips... and immediately reporting any malfunctions. 2. Standard warning signs and labels approved by SIRA must be placed at all main entrances and inside the elevators, alerting the presence of surveillance systems. 3. A record must be provided for each copying operation, containing all data related to the copying operation, who made it, where it was kept, or who received it, according to the approved form. 4. The time and date that all security systems operate on must be real, correct, and consistent with reality, and all the different parts of the systems must be synchronized and update the time and date value automatically and in accordance with the related systems operating in SIRA.'),
(56, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C4-LGT-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Four: Security Lighting', 'Security Lighting Controls', 'Security Lighting', '1', 28, 28, '1. Scenes within the range of surveillance cameras must be fully lit and free of any dark areas. 2. Invisible security lighting (infrared) may be used in secondary perimeter areas that are not primarily used or where visible light is insufficient for camera surveillance, provided that this lighting covers the range of vision of the surveillance cameras and that no infrared light is reflected in the camera. 3. The use of security lighting must not have any negative impact on the safety of others (Such as the effect of lighting on drivers\' vision).'),
(57, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C5-IMG-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Five: Image Acceptance', 'Image Clarity, Stability & Obstruction Limits', 'Image Acceptance & Visibility', '3', 28, 28, '1. The image must be clear, and its contents can be easily interpreted and read by the observer, and straight lines must be distinguishable without any image distortions. 2. The image should be stable and not shake even in moderate wind conditions. 3. The camera\'s field of view must be accessible and free of obstructions that obscure part of the image. An image will be considered unacceptable if the obstruction exceeds 5% of the total image area. The center of the image must be free of any obstructions, and the edges of the image must not exceed 5% of the total image area.'),
(58, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C6-SUS-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Six: The Sustainability of Security Systems', 'Physical Protection, Access Logs, Firewall & IK10 Vandal Resistance', 'Security System Sustainability', '8', 29, 29, '1. All digital recording devices must be installed in secure, clean, and constantly monitored locations. Access to them must be restricted to authorized personnel only... maintaining a continuous, auditable log containing details of entry, exit, and activities... and immediately notifying SIRA and maintenance company of any incident. 2. All security system connections must be independent and dedicated solely to serving the security systems... unless the connection is for integration purposes. In that case, a firewall must be provided to secure it after obtaining prior written approval from SIRA. 3. All active network components installed in secure locations with audited entry/exit log. 4. All wires hidden in conduits. 5. Tamper-proof electrical outlets. 6. Lightning protection where applicable. 7. Secure mounting. 8. If installation conditions require that security devices and equipment be installed within the reach of standard persons (1.6m) of less than 2.5 meters, then these security devices and equipment must be equipped with tamper-proof and vandal-proof features and shock-resistant features of no less than IK10 according to the international standard classification.'),
(59, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C7-MNT-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Seven: Maintenance, Development and Modification of Security Systems', 'Annual Maintenance Contract & Modification Notifications', 'Maintenance, Development & Modification', '1', 31, 31, '1. The facility is committed to entering an annual maintenance contract with one of the companies registered with SIRA. The contract must include a preventive maintenance program with no less than four visits per year, along with the legal response and penalties for failure to comply. The facility is responsible for notifying SIRA if it fails to implement the terms of the maintenance contract. 2. The user, facility, and maintenance and installation service provider are obliged to maintain a sustainable record and to notify SIRA when performing any work, procedure, or activity that results in a total or partial change, even if minor (11 enumerated change triggers including design, specs, programming, maps, lighting, obstructions, facility expansion/reduction, entrances/fences, business activity changes, adjacent projects). 3. The entire technical maintenance crew must be licensed by SIRA.'),
(60, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C8-PRH-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Eight: Prohibitions', 'Prohibited Surveillance Practices', 'Prohibitions', '1', 32, 32, '1. It is prohibited to use cameras with pan and zoom capabilities in private areas unless SIRA approval is obtained. 2. The use of hidden cameras is prohibited unless SIRA approval is obtained. 3. It is prohibited to install external cameras on the roof whose monitoring range exceeds the boundaries of the relevant facility unless SIRA approval is obtained.'),
(61, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C9-EXC-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Nine: Exceptional Cases', 'Shared Facilities, Minimum Standards & SIRA Authority', 'Exceptional Cases', '1', 32, 32, '1. If there are shared facilities or spaces in a facility that has more than one activity, the maximum requirements must be applied to them. 2. Everything mentioned in the Preventive Systems Manual is the minimum specifications and requirements that must be adhered to. Under no circumstances may equipment, installation, or implementation be carried out with specifications or requirements less than the minimum. It is not permissible to fail to adhere to any of its provisions except with official approval from SIRA. 3. SIRA may impose any additional security measures, security service, study, analysis, evaluation, specifications, requirements, design, or amendment... as it deems appropriate. 4. The installation of security devices and equipment must not cause the loss of security and safety requirements, such as fire-resistant doors or service outlets designed to prevent the spread of flames and fires.'),
(62, 'STANDARD', 'P2-C10-QUL-01', 'Part Two', 'Chapter Ten: Quality of Work and Installation', 'Workmanship, Labeling & Installation Safety', 'Installation Quality & Safety', '1', 33, 33, '1. The appearance must not be distorted by untidy security systems. Installation must be carried out within standard formal controls in terms of hiding or covering wires and using mounting bases specially manufactured for the purpose of installing security equipment. 2. All connections and wires must be numbered and marked on both sides with standard markings and numbers and manufactured specifically for this purpose. 3. Safety measures must be observed, individuals and property must not be harmed, and warning and guidance signs must be placed to avoid harming others.'),
